   10: ## G2-1 â€” the stamp fallback reaches agent files â€” ACCEPT
   11: 
   12: > "An ambiguous agent can be attributed from `$curStamp` instead of remaining
   13: > unattributed." (severity high, `loop/work/attribution-report.ps1:343`; the reader's
   14: > failure case: "An M1-style file with two item branches, then a stamp and a blank-branch
   15: > response has an empty tree item but reaches this stamp fallback, violating the required
   16: > 'degrade, never guess' behavior; A9 does not cover that state.")
   17: 
   18: Verified against the code. The counting loop updates `$curStamp` for EVERY file (line
   19: 329) and applies the stamp fallback for EVERY file (line 343). Plan D3 rules the stamp
   20: fallback for SESSION files only; an agent file resolves branch â†’ tree â†’ unattributed.
   21: The stamp regex deliberately matches the escaped form, so an agent transcript that
   22: quotes a stamp â€” in a spawn prompt or a tool result â€” sets `$curStamp`, and an ambiguous
   23: or unresolvable agent's branchless responses would then be guessed from it. That is the
   24: same defect class ruling G1-4 closed for the tree path, open on a second door.
